# Omni-Channel Inbox

Instagram Direct + Facebook Messenger for the CALL_CENTER role. Sibling of the
WhatsApp Chats page, deliberately **not** merged with it.

## What makes this different from WhatsApp Chats

- **A conversation is not a lead.** WhatsApp auto-creates a `Client` per inbound
  phone number (`ensure_client_for_whatsapp_phone`). The inbox does not: a DM
  creates `SocialContact` + `SocialConversation` only. `conversation.client` is
  `null` until an agent explicitly converts. Never add auto-creation here — most
  DMs are never worth a lead, and each one would charge the plan's `max_clients`
  quota.
- **A different Meta app.** `META_INBOX_*` settings, its own client id/secret,
  webhook verify token, and App Review lifecycle. The webhook signature is bound
  to `META_INBOX_CLIENT_SECRET` with **no** fallback to `META_CLIENT_SECRET`.
- **CALL_CENTER is allowed here and denied on WhatsApp.** Both rules are live at
  once and are pinned by `CRM-api-1/tests/test_call_center_permissions.py`. Do not
  "harmonize" them.

## Access control (backend-enforced, never client-only)

| Role | Sees |
|---|---|
| Owner / Admin | every company conversation |
| CALL_CENTER | every company conversation; may convert |
| Supervisor + `can_manage_social_inbox` | every company conversation |
| Employee / Doctor | only conversations whose converted lead is assigned to them |
| Reception / Data Entry | nothing (403) |

Unconverted DMs and `conversation.assigned_to` are **not** a visibility grant
for employee/doctor. If the lead is later reassigned, they lose the thread.

A conversation the viewer may not see answers **404, never 403** — a 403 would
confirm it exists. Keep it that way.

## Messaging window — stricter than WhatsApp

There are no approved templates to reopen a closed thread. Only two states send:

- within 24h of the last **inbound** message → `messaging_type: RESPONSE`
- 24h–7d → `messaging_type: MESSAGE_TAG` + `tag: HUMAN_AGENT`, **and only when
  `META_INBOX_HUMAN_AGENT_TAG_ENABLED` is on** (requires Meta approval of the
  Human Agent feature)

Outside that the API refuses with `social_outside_window` **before any Graph
call**, and deletes the pending row so a blocked attempt does not litter the
thread. The composer must render disabled from `GET /inbox/window/` rather than
letting an agent type a message that will be rejected. Never auto-send outside
the window — abusing the tag risks app-level enforcement against the whole app.

## Convert to lead

- Once only. A second attempt returns `409 social_already_converted` with the
  existing `client_id`; the UI shows the lead chip instead of erroring.
- **Phone is optional and must stay optional.** Instagram/Messenger carry no
  phone number. The created `Client` usually has `phone_number = None` and no
  `ClientPhoneNumber` row. That is safe against `uniq_company_phone_normalized`
  (the constraint is conditional on a non-empty normalized value). Never
  fabricate a placeholder number — it would consume the company-wide unique key.
- If a phone *is* supplied and matches an existing lead, the conversation links
  to that lead (`duplicate: true`) rather than forking a second one.
- Assignment reuses `crm/assignment.py`; notifications reuse
  `notify_lead_assignment_change` + `notify_owner_new_lead`, so an inbox lead
  behaves like every other inbound source.

## Freshness

The `inbox` sync slice is the primary refresh signal via
`useInvalidateOnSliceChange('inbox', …)`. `refetchInterval` is a backstop for a
dropped socket only — do not shorten it to compensate for a slice that is not
bumping; fix the bump instead. Bulk `update()` writes fire no `post_save`, so
mark-read bumps the slice explicitly (see `social_mark_conversation_read`).

## Page split

`pages/InboxPage.tsx` is the conversation UI. `components/integrations/
SocialInboxSection.tsx` is **connect/disconnect only** — no conversation UI in
Integrations, mirroring the WhatsApp precedent in `whatsapp-chats.mdc`.

### Shared chat primitives — reuse, do not import WA layout

Inbox reuses `components/chat/*` **as-is** (`ChatBlobMedia`, `ChatMediaViewer`,
`ChatConversationStatusMenu`, `ChatPendingAttachmentChip`,
`ChatVoiceRecordingBar`, `useChatVoiceRecorder`, `AttachmentSourceModal`,
`InboxFilterRail`) plus `whatsappChatTheme` tokens. Filter chrome (rail vs
chips, Channel vs Status sections) lives in `InboxFilterRail` and shares
visual tokens with WhatsApp via `components/chat/chatFilterRailChrome.tsx` —
never import `ChatFilterRail` itself. Thread status uses the same colored-dot
menu as WhatsApp Chats (open/pending/spam/invalid/done, snooze, star,
unsubscribe) — never a bare `<select>`. It must **not** import `ChatComposer`,
`ChatFilterRail`, `WhatsAppChatLayout`, `ConversationList`, `ChatThread`, or
`ChatMessageBubble` — those carry WhatsApp templates, lead-phone rows, and
calling. Keep the social send-window alerts and convert header Inbox-owned.

On the Meta page it renders as the **"Instagram & Messenger" tab**, beside "Lead
Ads" (`metaTab` state in `IntegrationsPage.tsx`). It deliberately reuses the Lead
Ads account-row shape — `Card p-0` + `divide-y` list, `IntegrationPlatformIcon` +
name + status pill, then `Connect` / `Edit` / `Disconnect` — so the two tabs
differ in content, not in furniture. The header's "Add New Account" button is
shown on both tabs and branches on `metaTab` to create the right platform.

### The account actions belong to the page, not the section

`onConnect` / `onEdit` / `onDisconnect` are passed in from `IntegrationsPage`.
The section owns only the per-Page rows. This is not decoration:

- **Connect must go through `openConnectPopup`.** Assigning `window.location` to
  the authorization URL works, but it throws the owner out of the CRM mid-task
  and there is then no opener for `OAuthCallbackPage` to `postMessage` back to —
  which is the handshake that refreshes the row in place. The popup is the
  mechanism, not a preference.
- **The inbox account is a separate query** (`socialInboxConnections`) from
  `connectedAccounts`. Anything that can change an account — OAuth success,
  OAuth failure, popup closed, rename, disconnect — has to invalidate both, or a
  freshly connected Page stays invisible until a manual reload. Use
  `invalidateAccountQueries()`.
- `handleDelete` resolves the account from `accounts` **or** the inbox query, so
  both tabs disconnect through the same confirm-then-revoke path.

A Page with no linked Instagram account is a supported setup (Messenger-only), so
`ig_user_id` is nullable and the UI shows an "Instagram not linked" state rather
than treating it as an error.

## The lead Timeline is a third surface

A converted conversation also appears on the lead's Timeline as a `social_thread`
card. It reads from its **own** endpoint —
`GET /integrations/inbox/lead-messages/?client=` via `useLeadSocialMessages` —
not from the Inbox conversation queries, because the timeline needs every message
across every conversation on the lead and none of the thread metadata.

- **That endpoint is gated on the inbox ACL, not on lead access.** Reception and
  data entry can open a lead and get **403** there. That is correct — they get
  nothing from the inbox by design — so `useLeadSocialMessages` sets
  `retry: false` and the timeline simply carries no social entries for them.
  Do not "fix" this by widening the endpoint's permission; that would put DM
  bodies in front of roles the inbox deliberately excludes.
- Rows carry `conversation` and `channel`, and
  `collapseConsecutiveSocialThreads` breaks a group when the conversation
  changes. A lead can hold an Instagram DM and a Messenger thread at once;
  grouping purely on adjacency would file two strangers under one heading.
- Any change here is bound by `lead-timeline-parity.mdc` — web and Flutter in
  one change set.

## Strings

Every user-facing string goes in `constants.ts` under both `en` and `ar` and is
rendered via `t()`. Check for an existing key before adding one — `viewLead` and
`unassigned` already exist and must not be duplicated.
